  "implementation_retained": [
    "Fourteen private normalization work counters attribute inclusive root-operation node growth and recursive depth entries to import, substitute, resolve, covariance opening/closing; plus memo/unchanged counts and variable-view/binder creation.",
    "No semantic authority, new map, source omission, type cache or representation change. Counters are cumulative work including rolled-back work.",
    "Keep the generic wide-record/nominal/effects executed guest as a semantic law; remove optimization-only native assertions and the rejected production implementation."
  ],
  "rejected_implementation": [
    "Reuse unchanged nodes during nonempty substitution only after complete child/row traversal and exact constructor checks. Allocate changed product/record/nominal output buffers lazily, retain per-use fresh rows/history and projection limits.",
    "Prototype passed four focused native laws including full OOM and both guest tiers with sync/JSPI and retained1\u21929\u21921 edits; baseline guests also passed.",
    "Reject: actual matrix/settings/render producer type-node reductions are below0.25%; checking time remains flat and matrix total regresses in these pairs. The118-line production expansion is not justified by this result."
  ],
  "review": "Astra xhigh: no prototype correctness blockers; reject it on real-source measurements. Zero extra views also rules out the proposed historical-view canonicalization on these workloads.",
  "method": "Three sequential alternating instrumented pairs; fresh sessions, cacheDirectory:false, five seconds per compile. All cells execute their independently expected inputs. Constructor attribution is one additional diagnostic sample per workload, not a latency distribution.",
